From 2b9122b2e1ab85068f56f4a91217647283dc6aa5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andras Lasso <lasso@queensu.ca>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:46:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] ENH: Let ray cast mappers intersect the pick ray in
 vtkMRMLAccuratePicker

Mappers that render surfaces without geometry that vtkCellPicker can
intersect (for example surfaces that are ray cast on the GPU) could not
be picked, so Shift+mouse move, Pick3D and painting in 3D views did not
work on them.

vtkMRMLRayCastMapper is a new abstract base class of such mappers, with a
pure virtual IntersectWithRay method: given the pick ray in the model
coordinates of the prop (from p1 to p2, between parametric coordinates t1
and t2), the mapper reports whether the ray hits its surface and the
parametric coordinate, position and normal of the first intersection.
vtkMRMLAccuratePicker calls it for actors whose mapper is a
vtkMRMLRayCastMapper, and reports the picked position and normal as for
cells (with no cell, data set or point IDs). Other mappers are picked by
intersecting their cells, as before.

vtkMRMLAccuratePickerTest checks picking of a minimal vtkMRMLRayCastMapper
in front of a mesh, and that a mapper that reports no intersection is not
picked.
